  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe transitive counterpart of {従|したが}う (to follow, to obey). While {従|したが}う describes the follower's action, {従|したが}える describes the leader's state of having followers. Often used in historical, formal, or literary contexts.\n\nGRAMMAR:\nTypically used in the pattern AがBを{従|したが}えて, where A is the leader and B is the follower(s).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {部下|ぶか}を{従|したが}える: to have subordinates in tow\n- {家来|けらい}を{従|したが}える: to be accompanied by retainers\n- {大軍|たいぐん}を{従|したが}える: to lead a large army\n- {弟子|でし}を{従|したが}える: to have disciples in tow",
